      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.69,
          "end": 2.04,
          "en": "Now with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 5.37,
          "en": "we added lots of features to this form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.37,
          "end": 7.8,
          "en": "more features than we added before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.8,
          "end": 9.54,
          "en": "with the template driven approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.54,
          "end": 13.77,
          "en": "because as you can see, with the reactive forms approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.77,
          "end": 16.38,
          "en": "adding features like custom validators",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.38,
          "end": 18.51,
          "en": "is super simple and straightforward.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.51,
          "end": 22.953,
          "en": "It's just a function we define and we then register and use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.88,
          "end": 27.15,
          "en": "Now let's see how we would implement that feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.15,
          "end": 29.79,
          "en": "where we saved the email address",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 29.79,
          "end": 33.45,
          "en": "and pre-populated that form with it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.45,
          "end": 36.03,
          "en": "And for that, here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.03,
          "end": 39.6,
          "en": "I will now actually use OnInit again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.6,
          "end": 42.96,
          "en": "I could also use afterNextRender again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.96,
          "end": 46.32,
          "en": "but here, I can also easily use ngOnInit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.32,
          "end": 51.32,
          "en": "because since I create my form here in my TypeScript class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.93,
          "end": 54.6,
          "en": "I don't need to wait for the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.6,
          "end": 57.51,
          "en": "to render for it to be initialized.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.51,
          "end": 60.09,
          "en": "Instead it is initialized right from the start",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.09,
          "end": 62.85,
          "en": "because I am initializing it in code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.85,
          "end": 64.71,
          "en": "That's another advantage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.71,
          "end": 67.74,
          "en": "of using the reactive forms approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.74,
          "end": 69.96000000000001,
          "en": "And therefore, here in ngOnInit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.96000000000001,
          "end": 73.41,
          "en": "we can start by setting up that subscription",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.41,
          "end": 76.98,
          "en": "where we want to save the updated form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.98,
          "end": 79.92,
          "en": "in the browser local storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.92,
          "end": 82.05,
          "en": "We do that just as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 82.05,
          "end": 85.11,
          "en": "We can use our forum and then valueChanges",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 85.11,
          "end": 88.8,
          "en": "and then subscribe to this observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 88.8,
          "end": 90.93,
          "en": "Now we don't need a question mark here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.93,
          "end": 94.14,
          "en": "because now, since we're using reactive forms",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.14,
          "end": 97.11,
          "en": "and we're setting up the form in our TypeScript code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 97.11,
          "end": 99.93,
          "en": "TypeScript knows that it will be initialized",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 99.93,
          "end": 103.233,
          "en": "and that we can safely set up this subscription.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.58,
          "end": 107.13,
          "en": "So then here I have my observer object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 107.13,
          "end": 110.46000000000001,
          "en": "and the next function where I get my value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 110.46000000000001,
          "end": 114.06,
          "en": "And now again, because we set up everything in TypeScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 114.06,
          "end": 117.3,
          "en": "TypeScript understands what the value looks like",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 117.3,
          "end": 120.543,
          "en": "and that it is an object of this shape in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 121.8,
          "end": 124.86,
          "en": "So in here, I now in the end therefore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 124.86,
          "end": 129.09,
          "en": "want to use my local storage to save this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 129.09,
          "end": 131.86,
          "en": "And again, I'll name it saved-login-form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 132.993,
          "end": 137.85,
          "en": "and I'll JSON.stringify my value here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 137.85,
          "end": 140.7,
          "en": "though, I actually just want to save the email,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 140.7,
          "end": 144.003,
          "en": "so I'll set it up like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 145.26,
          "end": 148.82999999999998,
          "en": "That's how I can save this form with every keystroke.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 148.82999999999998,
          "end": 150.48,
          "en": "Now, just as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 150.48,
          "end": 152.67000000000002,
          "en": "I don't want to do it with every keystroke,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 152.67000000000002,
          "end": 154.41,
          "en": "so I will call pipe here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 154.41,
          "end": 157.68,
          "en": "and use debounceTime, just as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 157.68,
          "end": 160.92000000000002,
          "en": "with a timeout of 500 milliseconds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 160.92000000000002,
          "end": 165.57,
          "en": "and debounceTime, of course, is imported from RXJS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 165.57,
          "end": 167.28,
          "en": "and we should also make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 167.28,
          "end": 169.38,
          "en": "that we clean up this subscription",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 169.38,
          "end": 172.17000000000002,
          "en": "to make sure that it's never going on behind the scenes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 172.17000000000002,
          "end": 174.3,
          "en": "if it shouldn't be going on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 174.3,
          "end": 177.6,
          "en": "So I'll store my subscription here in a constant,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 177.6,
          "end": 179.49,
          "en": "and just as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 179.49,
          "end": 183.52,
          "en": "I'll then also inject my destroyRef here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 185.07,
          "end": 190.07,
          "en": "with inject(DestroyRef) like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 191.79,
          "end": 193.74,
          "en": "And then in ngOnInit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 193.74,
          "end": 196.05,
          "en": "after setting up this subscription,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 196.05,
          "end": 200.16,
          "en": "we can register this onDestroy hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 200.16,
          "end": 203.133,
          "en": "and then here, clean up this subscription.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 204.42000000000002,
          "end": 208.82999999999998,
          "en": "With that, if we go to this application tab here, again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 208.82999999999998,
          "end": 210.273,
          "en": "you see if I reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 211.17000000000002,
          "end": 213.3,
          "en": "this is the initial value that's been saved.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 213.3,
          "end": 217.38,
          "en": "If I start typing here and then I stop at some point,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 217.38,
          "end": 220.983,
          "en": "after 500 milliseconds, this is updated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 222.03,
          "end": 224.52,
          "en": "So saving the value works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 224.52,
          "end": 228.513,
          "en": "Now let's update the form with any saved value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 230.78199999999998,
          "end": 234.48,
          "en": "And for that, in ngOnInit, just as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 234.48,
          "end": 236.85,
          "en": "we can of course get our saved form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 236.85,
          "end": 239.463,
          "en": "by accessing window.localStorage.getItem,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 240.48,
          "end": 243.72,
          "en": "and by using this key here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 243.72,
          "end": 244.89,
          "en": "And then just as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 244.89,
          "end": 247.68,
          "en": "I want to check if savedForm is truthy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 247.68,
          "end": 249.54,
          "en": "So if I found something there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 249.54,
          "end": 251.83,
          "en": "and then I can get my loadedForm",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 253.44,
          "end": 256.677,
          "en": "by using JSON.parse on that savedForm.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 257.97,
          "end": 260.85,
          "en": "And of course that will be an object of this shape,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 260.85,
          "end": 262.923,
          "en": "so an object with a email key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 264.75,
          "end": 268.29,
          "en": "So we can therefore now reach out to our form here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 268.29,
          "end": 272.553,
          "en": "and again, use setValue to update the overall form value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 273.84000000000003,
          "end": 277.2,
          "en": "or reach out to one of our controls",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 277.2,
          "end": 280.65,
          "en": "and just set the value of that control.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 280.65,
          "end": 283.65,
          "en": "Or when using the reactive forms approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 283.65,
          "end": 286.11,
          "en": "you actually also have an alternative method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 286.11,
          "end": 288.45,
          "en": "you can use on the overall form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 288.45,
          "end": 291.573,
          "en": "and that's the patchValue method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 292.86,
          "end": 295.35,
          "en": "This method is a method that exists",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 295.35,
          "end": 299.313,
          "en": "if you want to partially update an overall form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 300.78,
          "end": 303.66,
          "en": "And patchValue then wants an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 303.66,
          "end": 307.02,
          "en": "that can have the shape of your form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 307.02,
          "end": 310.263,
          "en": "So the key value pairs you registered in your form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 311.37,
          "end": 313.8,
          "en": "But I'm saying can because you can add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 313.8,
          "end": 316.5,
          "en": "as many key value pairs as you need.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 316.5,
          "end": 320.19,
          "en": "For example, here, I can only set the email control.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 320.19,
          "end": 322.89,
          "en": "And now you set that to a new value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 322.89,
          "end": 326.01,
          "en": "which could be a new string, a new empty string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 326.01,
          "end": 329.49,
          "en": "or in my case, loadedForm.email,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 329.49,
          "end": 333.063,
          "en": "which I know will be such a string value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 334.14,
          "end": 336.48,
          "en": "And now patchValue will make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 336.48,
          "end": 339.63,
          "en": "that only this control receives a new value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 339.63,
          "end": 342.783,
          "en": "and all the other controls will stay untouched.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 343.8,
          "end": 346.5,
          "en": "With that, if I save that and if I reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 346.5,
          "end": 348.963,
          "en": "this is still pre-populated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 350.25,
          "end": 354.24,
          "en": "Now, if I delete saved log in form from my local storage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 354.24,
          "end": 357.723,
          "en": "and I reload, you see we start with an empty form instead,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 358.68,
          "end": 360.99,
          "en": "but then again, we can start typing in there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 360.99,
          "end": 363.66,
          "en": "this gets saved and if we reload again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 363.66,
          "end": 366.093,
          "en": "this is pre-populated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 367.2,
          "end": 370.08,
          "en": "So that's now working the way it should.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 370.08,
          "end": 373.86,
          "en": "But since we're using the reactive forms approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 373.86,
          "end": 378.063,
          "en": "we could even load and populate our form in a different way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 379.2,
          "end": 383.46,
          "en": "Instead of using this approach, which is absolutely fine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 383.46,
          "end": 388.08,
          "en": "we could also load our content from local storage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 388.08,
          "end": 392.55,
          "en": "right when this file here is about to be executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 392.55,
          "end": 396.69,
          "en": "So totally detached from our component lifecycle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 396.69,
          "end": 398.79,
          "en": "Let's say here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 398.79,
          "end": 400.863,
          "en": "So outside of the component code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 402.36,
          "end": 407.36,
          "en": "And we can parse the JSON content right below that line,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 408.72,
          "end": 411.033,
          "en": "also outside of the component code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 411.9,
          "end": 414.06,
          "en": "Though now here, TypeScript complains",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 414.06,
          "end": 416.47,
          "en": "that savedForm could be null",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 417.54,
          "end": 419.61,
          "en": "because we also need that if check of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 419.61,
          "end": 422.463,
          "en": "to check if savedForm is truthy.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 424.11,
          "end": 427.143,
          "en": "And we could then add a variable here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 427.143,
          "end": 430.383,
          "en": "initialEmailValue, which could be an empty string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 431.22,
          "end": 436.22,
          "en": "but which I set to that loadedForm email value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 436.77,
          "end": 440.07,
          "en": "so to the email value stored in local storage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 440.07,
          "end": 442.413,
          "en": "if I have some stored value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 443.46,
          "end": 446.34,
          "en": "And I'm doing all that here outside of the component,",
